Sending keys: ['cat > /app/output/answer.txt <<\'EOF\'\n## Statute\n\nSection 2(b)(2)(B) (line 230):\n"(B) a taxpayer shall be considered as not married at the close of his taxable year if at any time during the taxable year his spouse is a nonresident alien; and"\n\nSection 2(b)(2)(C) (line 232):\n"(C) a taxpayer shall be considered as married at the close of his taxable year if his spouse (other than a spouse described in subparagraph (B)) died during the taxable year."\n\n## Reasoning\n\nThe facts state:\n- Alice and Bob got married on Feb 3rd, 1992\n- Alice died on July 9th, 2014\n\nSection 2(b)(2)(C) states that a taxpayer shall be considered as married at the close of his taxable year if his spouse died during the taxable year, but only if the spouse is NOT described in subparagraph (B).\n\nSection 2(b)(2)(B) states that a taxpayer is considered not married if his spouse is a nonresident alien at any time during the taxable year.\n\nThe case facts do not state that Alice was a nonresident alien at any time during 2014. Therefore, Alice is not described in §2(b)(2)(B), and the exception does not apply.\n\nAlice died on July 9th, 2014, which is during the taxable year 2014. Since Alice died during 2014 and she was not a nonresident alien, Section 2(b)(2)(C) applies to Bob in 2014.\n\n## Answer\nAnswer: Entailment\nEOF\n'] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
