Sending keys: ['cat > /app/output/answer.txt << \'EOF\'\n## Statute\n\n§1(c) Unmarried individuals (other than surviving spouses and heads of households):\n"There is hereby imposed on the taxable income of every individual (other than a surviving spouse as defined in section 2(a) or the head of a household as defined in section 2(b)) who is not a married individual (as defined in section 7703) a tax determined in accordance with the following:\n    (v) $79,772, plus 39.6% of the excess over $250,000 if the taxable income is over $250,000."\nLine: §1(c) at line 80-81, §1(c)(v) at line 85\n\n§162(c)(2)(C) Basic standard deduction:\n"(C) $3,000 in any other case."\nLine: §162(c)(2)(C) at line 396\n\n§151(d)(1) Exemption amount:\n"the term \'exemption amount\' means $2,000."\nLine: §151(d)(1) at line 69\n\n§151(d)(3)(B) Applicable percentage:\n"the term \'applicable percentage\' means 2 percentage points for each $2,500 (or fraction thereof) by which the taxpayer\'s adjusted gross income for the taxable year exceeds the applicable amount in effect under section 68(b)."\nLine: §151(d)(3)(B) at line 82-84\n\n§68(b)(1)(C) Applicable amount:\n"$250,000 in the case of an individual who is not married and who is not a surviving spouse or head of household"\nLine: §68(b)(1)(C) at line 489\n\n## Reasoning\n\nCase Facts:\n- Alice is unmarried (her father Bob is not her spouse)\n- Alice\'s gross income in 2015: $311,510\n- Bob has no income in 2015\n- Alice takes the standard deduction\n\n1. Filing Status: Alice is an unmarried individual under §1(c)\n\n2. Standard Deduction: Under §162(c)(2)(C), the basic standard deduction for "any other case" (unmarried) is $3,000.\n\n3. Personal Exemption: Under §151(d)(1), the exemption amount is $2,000.\n\n4. Phaseout Calculation: Under §151(d)(3)(A), the exemption is reduced if AGI exceeds the applicable amount under §68(b).\n   - Applicable amount for unmarried under §68(b)(1)(C): $250,000\n   - Alice\'s AGI: $311,510\n   - Excess: $311,510 - $250,000 = $61,510\n   - Increments of $2,500: ceil($61,510 / $2,500) = 25\n   - Applicable percentage: 2% × 25 = 50%\n   - Exemption after phaseout: $2,000 × (1 - 0.50) = $1,000\n\n5. Taxable Income: $311,510 - $3,000 - $1,000 = $307,510\n\n6. Tax Calculation under §1(c)(v):\n   - Tax = $79,772 + 39.6% × ($307,510 - $250,000)\n   - Tax = $79,772 + 0.396 × $57,510\n   - Tax = $79,772 + $22,773.96\n   - Tax = $102,545.96\n   - Rounded: $102,546\n\n## Answer\nAnswer: 102546\nEOF\n'] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
